# The real DSS header of hdrcases/real_dss_plate_solution with its PLATEID
# card moved after the plate keywords (round-3 verifier probe
# probedss/dss_plateid_last). wcslib 8.10's lexer sets distran = 0 when it
# meets PLATEID ("insufficient to trigger DSS"), so with PLATEID last no
# distortion type is set and wcsset REFUSES the header although every
# plate keyword is present (with PLATEID before them, as the archive
# writes it, the later AMDXm cards set distran = DSS again). A card's
# position must not change a header's meaning (FITS Standard 4.0 sect.
# 4.4.1: keyword order is free apart from the mandatory keywords), so we
# apply the plate solution, and the answer must equal the golden of
# real_dss_plate_solution.
# EXPECT-WCSLIB-ERROR: No distortion type, yet DQia keyvalues are present
# SAME-AS: real_dss_plate_solution
NOTE lenient: dss_plateid_last
GRID 1 100 9 1 100 9
HEADER
SIMPLE  =                    T /FITS header
BITPIX  =                   16 /No.Bits per pixel
NAXIS   =                    2 /No.dimensions
NAXIS1  =                  100 /Length X axis
NAXIS2  =                  100 /Length Y axis
EXTEND  =                    T /
DATE    = '10/01/21          ' /Date of FITS file creation
ORIGIN  = 'CASB -- STScI     ' /Origin of FITS image
PLTLABEL= 'J 2098            ' /Observatory plate label
REGION  = 'S134              ' /GSSS Region Name
DATE-OBS= '11/03/76          ' /UT date of Observation
UT      = '17:38:00.00       ' /UT time of observation
EPOCH   =  1.9761932373047E+03 /Epoch of plate
PLTRAH  =                   14 /Plate center RA
PLTRAM  =                   37 /
PLTRAS  =  4.6882530000000E+01 /
PLTDECSN= '-                 ' /Plate center Dec
PLTDECD =                   60 /
PLTDECM =                   12 /
PLTDECS =  5.9287610000000E+01 /
EQUINOX =  2.0000000000000E+03 /Julian Reference frame equinox
EXPOSURE=  7.0000000000000E+01 /Exposure time minutes
BANDPASS=                    0 /GSSS Bandpass code
PLTGRADE=                    1 /Plate grade
PLTSCALE=  6.7200000000000E+01 /Plate Scale arcsec per mm
SITELAT = '-31:16:24.00      ' /Latitude of Observatory
SITELONG= '+149:03:42.00     ' /Longitude of Observatory
TELESCOP= 'UK 48-inch Schmidt' /Telescope where plate taken
CNPIX1  =                 8860 /X corner  (pixels)
CNPIX2  =                 1708 /Y corner
DATATYPE= 'INTEGER*2         ' /Type of Data
